# Breakout, in Intent v0.6.0.
#   ./intent build gemini-build/build-10-breakout/breakout.intent -o build/breakout && build/breakout
# Left/right move the paddle. Clear all bricks for the next level. q quits, enter plays again.
#
# The ball is four single values (where it is, which way it goes). Bricks are a collection
# that is only ever compared with single values, which Intent 0.6 can do.
# Each brick is 3 cells wide: it is stored by its left edge and drawn three times.

The board is 30 wide and 18 high.

The paddle starts at 15.
The ball x starts at 15.
The ball y starts at 14.
The dx starts at 1.
The dy starts at -1.
The next x starts at 0.
The next y starts at 0.
The broke starts at 0.
The score starts at 0.
The lives start at 3.
The level starts at 1.
The refill starts at 0.

Bricks is a collection where each brick has an x (number), a y (number) and a toughness (number).

Start with a brick at x 2, y 3, toughness 2.
Start with a brick at x 6, y 3, toughness 2.
Start with a brick at x 10, y 3, toughness 2.
Start with a brick at x 14, y 3, toughness 2.
Start with a brick at x 18, y 3, toughness 2.
Start with a brick at x 22, y 3, toughness 2.
Start with a brick at x 26, y 3, toughness 2.
Start with a brick at x 2, y 5, toughness 1.
Start with a brick at x 6, y 5, toughness 1.
Start with a brick at x 10, y 5, toughness 1.
Start with a brick at x 14, y 5, toughness 1.
Start with a brick at x 18, y 5, toughness 1.
Start with a brick at x 22, y 5, toughness 1.
Start with a brick at x 26, y 5, toughness 1.

# --- the paddle is 5 wide, centred on the paddle value
When the left key is pressed, the paddle decreases by 2 if the paddle is over 3.
When the right key is pressed, the paddle increases by 2 if the paddle is under 28.

# --- one step of the ball, in order
# 1. where would it go?
Every 70 milliseconds, the next x becomes the ball x plus the dx.
Every 70 milliseconds, the next y becomes the ball y plus the dy.
# 2. walls turn it
Every 70 milliseconds, if the next x is under 1 or the next x is over 30, the dx becomes 0 minus the dx.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the next y is under 1, the dy becomes 0 minus the dy.
Every 70 milliseconds, the next x becomes the ball x plus the dx.
Every 70 milliseconds, the next y becomes the ball y plus the dy.
# 3. a brick in the way: wear it down, bounce
Every 70 milliseconds, if any brick has an x at most the next x and an x at least the next x minus 2 and a y equal to the next y, the broke becomes 1.
Every 70 milliseconds, decrease the toughness of the bricks whose x is at most the next x and whose x is at least the next x minus 2 and whose y is the next y by 1.
Every 70 milliseconds, remove the bricks whose toughness is under 1.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the broke is 1, the score increases by the level.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the broke is 1, the dy becomes 0 minus the dy.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the broke is 1, the broke becomes 0.
# 4. the paddle sends it back up, and the side it lands on steers it
Every 70 milliseconds, if the next y is 18 and the next x is at least the paddle minus 2 and the next x is at most the paddle plus 2, the dy becomes -1.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the next y is 18 and the next x is at least the paddle minus 2 and the next x is under the paddle, the dx becomes -1.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the next y is 18 and the next x is over the paddle and the next x is at most the paddle plus 2, the dx becomes 1.
# 5. move
Every 70 milliseconds, the ball x increases by the dx.
Every 70 milliseconds, the ball y increases by the dy.
# 6. missed: lose a life, serve again
Every 70 milliseconds, if the ball y is over 18, the lives decrease by 1.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the ball y is over 18, the ball x becomes the paddle.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the ball y is over 18, the dy becomes -1.
Every 70 milliseconds, if the ball y is over 18, the ball y becomes 16.

# --- a cleared wall: next level, tougher bricks
Every 100 milliseconds, if no brick has a y over 0, the refill becomes 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, the level increases by 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 2, whose y is 2 and whose toughness is the level.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 8, whose y is 3 and whose toughness is the level.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 14, whose y is 2 and whose toughness is the level.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 20, whose y is 3 and whose toughness is the level.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 26, whose y is 2 and whose toughness is the level.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 5, whose y is 5 and whose toughness is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 11, whose y is 6 and whose toughness is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 17, whose y is 5 and whose toughness is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, add a brick whose x is 23, whose y is 6 and whose toughness is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the refill is 1, the refill becomes 0.

The game is over when the lives are under 1.

# --- what you see
Draw each brick whose toughness is 1 at its x and its y as a green "=".
Draw each brick whose toughness is 1 at its x plus 1 and its y as a green "=".
Draw each brick whose toughness is 1 at its x plus 2 and its y as a green "=".
Draw each brick whose toughness is over 1 at its x and its y as a red "#".
Draw each brick whose toughness is over 1 at its x plus 1 and its y as a red "#".
Draw each brick whose toughness is over 1 at its x plus 2 and its y as a red "#".
Draw a white "=" at the paddle minus 2 and 18.
Draw a white "=" at the paddle minus 1 and 18.
Draw a white "=" at the paddle and 18.
Draw a white "=" at the paddle plus 1 and 18.
Draw a white "=" at the paddle plus 2 and 18.
Draw a yellow "o" at the ball x and the ball y.
Show the score, the lives and the level above the board.
